LETTER DESCRIPTION/CONTENT EXAMPLES
    EXAMPLE 1:
        IN THE MATTER OF THE ESTATE OF ROBERT J. THOMPSON
        CASE NO. 2024-PR-1234

        ORDER GRANTING LETTERS OF ADMINISTRATION

        This matter coming before the Court on the petition of Michael Thompson for Letters of Administration, and the Court being fully advised in the premises, it is hereby ORDERED that Michael Thompson is appointed as Administrator of the Estate of Robert J. Thompson, deceased.

        The Administrator is authorized to take possession of all assets, pay just debts, and distribute the remaining estate according to law. Bond is fixed in the amount of $500,000.

        Dated: March 15, 2024
        Hon. Sarah Mitchell
        Probate Court Judge
    EXAMPLE 2:
        NOTICE OF HEARING ON PETITION FOR FINAL DISTRIBUTION

        TO: ALL INTERESTED PERSONS AND BENEFICIARIES

        NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a hearing on the Petition for Final Distribution of the Estate of Margaret Williams will be held on April 20, 2024, at 9:00 AM in Courtroom 3B of the Superior Court.

        Any objections to the proposed distribution must be filed with the Court no later than 5 days prior to the hearing date.

        /s/ Clerk of Court
    EXAMPLE 3:
        RE: ESTATE OF JAMES PATRICK O'CONNOR - FILE #2023-PR-0892

        Dear Beneficiaries,

        This letter serves to inform you that the probate proceedings for the above-referenced estate have been completed. The final accounting has been approved by the Court, and distribution of assets will commence within 30 days.

        Please ensure your current contact information is on file with the Administrator to receive your distribution.

        Sincerely,
        Jennifer Walsh
        Estate Administrator

